 from the telltale games to  the joker according to what i've been  told they're gonna be shown as basically  politicians that starve the people of  gotham in order to line their pockets  bruce discovering this is what sets him  on a path to right the wrongs of the  past and he realizes that he must do  better and change the legacy that they  left behind according to huff reeve said  it's a detective story that's incredibly  personal so this idea of the waynes  being involved does make a lot of sense  from what i've heard on people close to  the film the riddler will very much be  an outcast in gotham that has decided to  clean up the corruption within it and  this is why he's carrying out  high-profile murders on people like the  mayor and d.a this is something that we  saw in batman earth 1 vol 2 and the  riddler was sort of an anti-hero who was  committing crimes for the greater good  of gotham now over the top of this we  could catch batman mercilessly beating  people up in a dark prison set with a  shining red light over the top of it i  absolutely love this idea of batman  being very unhinged and from the first  look it seemed like the character was  very much obsessed with being in this  persona in prior batman movies we've had  a lot of balance between the bruce wayne  and batman personalities but here it  seems like he's just completely focused  on being the dark knight we have seen  something similar in not only the earth  1 storyline but also in the new 52 run  by scott snyder both were filled with  b-boy pretty much casting bruce to the  side so that he could focus solely on  being batman however by the end of the  work he realized how important it was to  have balance so that people would stop  asking questions and also that he had a  way to infiltrate the gotham elite  through other means most importantly it  was just great for his mental health and  instead of hanging around in the cave  all day or running on rooftops at night  he did have an outlet now it has been  said that the film will focus heavily on  batman's mental health and that it won't  paint him out as some amazing hero  instead he will be conflicted and though  he's pretty much you know a good guy  from what i've been told there'll also  be a strong argument that he's a  complete psychopath this was of course  reflected in his most famous villain the  joker and his solo movie now i'm not  saying yet before you start yet i'm not  saying that arthur fleck was a good guy  quite the opposite but he very much  represented a person that people could  rally behind and in that story at least  he was painted out as the hero of it  even though the argument exists that  he's not which yet again i'm not saying  arthur is a good guy stop the hashtag  heavy spoilers over party now from here  on we apparently got several explosions  police officers and chaos spilling out  into gotham pattinson said he's really  working out his rage and that all the  fights are personal according to what  we've shown we could catch him brutally  beating people with numerous weapons  including pipes and he smashed their  heads in like you should smash that like  button go on do it  now this was all pretty much shown in  the first trailer but cinemacon did drop  an exclusive look at alfred who davis  described as a classy looking gentleman  wearing a vest over his shirt they've  kept the bottle mans look close to the  vest butterman and we still haven't seen  him but there's a couple of fan images  out there that could potentially show  exactly what he looks like we now have  it confirmed that he will have white  hair so yeah just just look at these and  imagine that it's real now from here the  attendees were shown some shots of the  batmobile driving and there were flames  coming out of the exhaust that was  pretty much all we got but i think it's  you know we can take a lot from this and  they're clearly trying to establish this  world that's very dark and gritty now  what i love